    definition: "Gender is the grouping of nouns according to whether they are regarded as male, female or without sex. Traditional grammar names four kinds: masculine, feminine, common and neuter. Masculine gender names male beings (father, uncle, author) and feminine gender names female beings (girl, mother, aunt).",
